        "purpose": "transcribing",
        "value": "河村藏主"
      },
      {
        "purpose": "modern_jp_reading",
        "value": "河村蔵主（かわむら くらぬし／reading conjectural）"
      },
      {
        "purpose": "english_translation",
        "value": "Kawamura Kuranushi (reading conjectural), an officer of Akashi. His name stands alone in a column that carries no label of its own: a sweep of x1290-1430 from y900 to y1975 finds no ink even at a grey threshold of 190. The column lies between the acting senior councillors' column on the right and the junior councillor label on the left, and which office he held is not settled by the page. Everywhere else in Fascicle 9 an office's names begin in its own label column and any further names run leftward into label-less columns — including the senior councillor of Akizuki lower on this same leaf, and 權大參事 三員 on the following leaf lower_p221_left (printed page 419), whose third name sits in exactly such a label-less column. That convention would make this man a third acting senior councillor, against the printed 二人. The alternative is that he is the one named junior councillor of four and that the 少參事 label was set one column too far left. The page carries no editorial correction either way."
      },
      {
        "purpose": "identifying",
        "value": "少参事河村藏主"
      }
    ],
